Title:
sliver-psh — PowerShell in-memory stager for Sliver beacons (AES-encrypted over HTTP + AMSI patch)

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
This repository provides a PowerShell stager for Sliver C2 that downloads an AES-256-CBC encrypted beacon over HTTP, decrypts it in memory, and executes it without writing the payload to disk. It includes a generated, XOR-obfuscated AMSI patch that modifies `AmsiScanBuffer` in the current PowerShell process to return `E_INVALIDARG`, effectively skipping AMSI scanning before payload execution. Execution is performed via `Marshal.GetDelegateForFunctionPointer` (function-pointer delegate) rather than creating a new thread, reducing common telemetry tied to thread creation. The loader allocates memory as RW, copies shellcode, then flips to RX to avoid RWX pages. An optional `mshta.exe` HTA dropper is included as one delivery method, but the stager can be used with any PowerShell cradle. It’s primarily useful for red teams/pentesters running Sliver who want an encrypted, fileless staging path with basic AMSI neutralization.

Technical Focus:
- Sliver C2 beacon generation (shellcode profiles, mTLS listener)
- PowerShell in-memory shellcode loading and execution (delegates/function pointers)
- AES-256-CBC payload encryption/decryption workflow (key/IV handling)
- AMSI bypass via patching `AmsiScanBuffer` in-process
- Memory protection transitions (RW → RX) to avoid RWX allocations
- HTA (`mshta.exe`) based initial execution / download cradle delivery

Use Cases:
- Fileless staging of Sliver beacons in Windows environments
- Encrypting staged payloads at rest/in transit over simple HTTP hosting
- Testing AMSI-focused detections against in-process patch techniques
- Phishing-style initial access simulation using HTA + PowerShell cradle
- Red team tradecraft for reducing disk artifacts and some common telemetry

Keywords:
Sliver, PowerShell stager, in-memory execution, shellcode loader, AES-256-CBC, HTTP download cradle, mTLS, AMSI, AmsiScanBuffer, E_INVALIDARG, XOR obfuscation, P/Invoke, Marshal.GetDelegateForFunctionPointer, VirtualProtect, RW to RX, mshta.exe, HTA dropper, fileless, beacon staging